IMPORT prelude

-- Property Tax Act 1960 (Singapore), s 9(2) -- the progressive rates for owner-occupied residential property, set by the
-- Minister's order under s 9(2) instead of the statutory 36% in s 9(1).
--
-- SOURCE: NOT THE ORDER. The bands and rates are as published by IRAS on "Lower property tax rates for owner-occupied
-- residential properties" (https://www.iras.gov.sg/taxes/property-tax/property-owners/property-tax-reliefs/
-- lower-property-tax-rates-for-owner-occupied-residential-properties), read on 10 October 2026. The page cites only the
-- Property Tax Act. The s 9(2) order that actually prescribes these rates was not retrieved. Each table's cumulative column was
-- checked against the bands and rates (all agree), and the page's three worked examples are asserted as cases.
--
-- WHY. Added on 11 October 2026 for REQ-0010 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl (cradle-to-grave-simone, event e072: the tax
-- for 2032 on an owner-occupied HDB flat with an annual value of $12,000).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: who qualifies as owner-occupier (an IRAS approval, here an input); the non-owner-occupied residential rates;
-- rebates and the s 6(5) $18 floor (ptx-core.l4 has the floor); part-year owner-occupation; years before 2015.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human
-- gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Owner-occupier rates under s 9(2), as published by IRAS`

-- The part of `av` lying between `from` and `to`.
GIVEN av IS A NUMBER, from IS A NUMBER, to IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the slice of` av from to MEANS
    IF av AT MOST from THEN 0
    ELSE IF av AT MOST to THEN av MINUS from ELSE to MINUS from

GIVETH A NUMBER
`no upper limit` MEANS 1000000000000

-- From 1 January 2025: 0% on the first $12,000; 4% to $40,000; 6% to $50,000; 10% to $75,000; 14% to $85,000; 20% to
-- $100,000; 26% to $140,000; 32% above.
GIVEN av IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the 2025 owner-occupier tax` av MEANS
          `the slice of` av 12000 40000 TIMES 0.04
    PLUS  `the slice of` av 40000 50000 TIMES 0.06
    PLUS  `the slice of` av 50000 75000 TIMES 0.10
    PLUS  `the slice of` av 75000 85000 TIMES 0.14
    PLUS  `the slice of` av 85000 100000 TIMES 0.20
    PLUS  `the slice of` av 100000 140000 TIMES 0.26
    PLUS  `the slice of` av 140000 `no upper limit` TIMES 0.32

-- 2024: 0% on the first $8,000; 4% to $30,000; 6% to $40,000; 10% to $55,000; 14% to $70,000; 20% to $85,000; 26% to
-- $100,000; 32% above.
GIVEN av IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the 2024 owner-occupier tax` av MEANS
          `the slice of` av 8000 30000 TIMES 0.04
    PLUS  `the slice of` av 30000 40000 TIMES 0.06
    PLUS  `the slice of` av 40000 55000 TIMES 0.10
    PLUS  `the slice of` av 55000 70000 TIMES 0.14
    PLUS  `the slice of` av 70000 85000 TIMES 0.20
    PLUS  `the slice of` av 85000 100000 TIMES 0.26
    PLUS  `the slice of` av 100000 `no upper limit` TIMES 0.32

-- 2023: same bands as 2024; 4, 5, 7, 10, 14, 18, 23%.
GIVEN av IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the 2023 owner-occupier tax` av MEANS
          `the slice of` av 8000 30000 TIMES 0.04
    PLUS  `the slice of` av 30000 40000 TIMES 0.05
    PLUS  `the slice of` av 40000 55000 TIMES 0.07
    PLUS  `the slice of` av 55000 70000 TIMES 0.10
    PLUS  `the slice of` av 70000 85000 TIMES 0.14
    PLUS  `the slice of` av 85000 100000 TIMES 0.18
    PLUS  `the slice of` av 100000 `no upper limit` TIMES 0.23

-- 2015 to 2022: 0% on the first $8,000; 4% to $55,000; 6% to $70,000; 8% to $85,000; 10% to $100,000; 12% to $115,000;
-- 14% to $130,000; 16% above.
GIVEN av IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the 2015 to 2022 owner-occupier tax` av MEANS
          `the slice of` av 8000 55000 TIMES 0.04
    PLUS  `the slice of` av 55000 70000 TIMES 0.06
    PLUS  `the slice of` av 70000 85000 TIMES 0.08
    PLUS  `the slice of` av 85000 100000 TIMES 0.10
    PLUS  `the slice of` av 100000 115000 TIMES 0.12
    PLUS  `the slice of` av 115000 130000 TIMES 0.14
    PLUS  `the slice of` av 130000 `no upper limit` TIMES 0.16

-- The tax for a year (2015 onwards) on a residential property occupied by its owner for the whole year. Later years
-- assume the 2025 rates still apply: no order changing them was known on 10 October 2026.
GIVEN av IS A NUMBER, year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the owner-occupier property tax` av year MEANS
    IF year AT LEAST 2025 THEN `the 2025 owner-occupier tax` av
    ELSE IF year EQUALS 2024 THEN `the 2024 owner-occupier tax` av
         ELSE IF year EQUALS 2023 THEN `the 2023 owner-occupier tax` av
              ELSE `the 2015 to 2022 owner-occupier tax` av
